  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Publication" is an exhibition held at Nigel Greenwood, London, 1970, which consisted of multiple copies of David Lamelas' book of the same name. David Lamelas issued the following three statements to thirteen artists: 1. Use of oral and written language as an Art Form. 2. Language can be considered as an Art Form. 3. Language can not be considered as an Art Form. The book presents responses to these statements from Keith Arnatt, Robert Barry, Stanley Brouwn, Daniel Buren, Victor Burgin, Michel Claura, Gilbert and George, John Latham, Lucy Lippard, Martin Maloney, Barbara M. Reise, Lawrence Weiner and Ian Wilson. - "Originally published in 1970 by Nigel Greenwood Ltd."--Colophon. - Printed in an edition of 1,000. - Includes bibliographical references. - Text in English or French</subfield>
  </datafield>
